From: Manchego Stars engine
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] Arena (#265): battle fade-in and palette cycle share campaign backdrop data

Install the campaign-agnostic Arena combat palette seam at fade-in.

Notes:

It makes the Arena battle fade-in use the same palette pointer array as its cycle.
---
diff --git a/src/banim-ekrarena.c b/src/banim-ekrarena.c
index c1138d51e66d17a1a02c35fcdda32f4767f3c0cb..edf337109ea6a917286702ab9071b0fde037776d 100644
--- a/src/banim-ekrarena.c
+++ b/src/banim-ekrarena.c
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #include "ekrbattle.h"
 #include "constants/songs.h"
 
+extern u16 * CONST_DATA PalArray_ArenaBattleBg[];
+
 EWRAM_DATA int gBaArenaFlag = 0;
 
 //! FE8U = 0x0805B01C
@@ -125,7 +127,7 @@ void ekrTogiInit_Init(ProcPtr proc)
     NewEkrDispUP();
     NewEkrBattle();
 
-    CpuFastCopy(Pal_ArenaBattleBg_A, gPaletteBuffer + 0x60, 0x80);
+    CpuFastCopy(PalArray_ArenaBattleBg[0], gPaletteBuffer + 0x60, 0x80);
     CpuFastCopy(gPaletteBuffer, gEfxPal, 0x400);
     CpuFastCopy(gEfxPal, gPaletteBuffer, 0x400);
     EfxPalBlackInOut(gPaletteBuffer, 0, 0x20, 0x10);
